-- title:
--   Adelic Brandt-matrix count for a left-stable Hecke set
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is finitely generated. Write $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}=\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{f}}$ for the tensor product with the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$, let $\widehat R\subseteq\widehat{\mathbb{H}}$ be the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every place, and let $U=$ [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) be the stabiliser of $\widehat R$ in $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$. Let $T\subseteq\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$ be a set satisfying $uh\in T$ for all $u\in U$ and $h\in T$, and let $x,y\in\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$. For $g\in\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$ put $I_g=$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele R g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19), the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ pulled back from $g\widehat R$ along the inclusion $\mathbb{H}\hookrightarrow\widehat{\mathbb{H}}$. The assertion is that the Hecke kernel [`QuaternionAlgebra.heckeKernel`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_ClassSetHecke.html#L66) of $U$ and $T$ at the pair of double cosets $\mathbb{H}^{\times}xU$, $\mathbb{H}^{\times}yU$ — that is, the integer obtained from the number of cosets $hU$ with $h\in T$ such that $x'h$ and $y$ have the same double coset, $x'$ being the chosen representative of the class of $x$ — equals the number of $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules $J$ of $\mathbb{H}$ such that $J=I_{xh}$ for some $h\in T$ and $J=d\cdot I_y$ for some $d\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$.
--
--   This is the adelic half of Eichler's description of Brandt matrix entries: the Hecke incidence number between two classes in $\mathbb{H}^{\times}\backslash\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}/\widehat R^{\times}$ is computed as a count of right $R$-lattices in the class of $I_y$ arising from $T$, the only property of $T$ used being stability under left multiplication by $\widehat R^{\times}$. It is used in the comparison of Hecke matrices on the quaternionic side with those coming from the Čerednik–Drinfel'd description of the relevant moduli, at primes dividing the level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_heckeKernel_mk_mk_eq_natCard_of_forall_mul_mem.lean

import Mathlib
